 the atmosphere so2 is the symbol  for sulfur dioxide and then NOx and Oh X  is the symbol for nitrogen oxides these  tend to be in the app guesses are  released into the atmosphere and when  they're in the atmosphere they tend to  react with rainwater whenever it rains  and when when these gases react with  rainwater they turn into sulfuric acid  and nitric acid and of course as it  continues to rain these acids get  basically washed down to the surface  down to the ground and they mix in  rivers and lakes and streams and they  absorb into the soil of the earth so  where do these sulfur dioxides and  nitrogen oxides that are in the  atmosphere come from well a natural  source would be volcanoes you know when  volcanoes erupt these are some of the  gas gases that are released into the  atmosphere as the volcano erupts but I  think the reason we're watching this  video is to try to understand the  man-made causes of acid rain and we see  it in the burning of fossil fuels now in  this picture here of an of a tailpipe of  the exhaust pipe of the automobile that  dioxis all four die oxides and nitrogen  oxides are released in the exhaust of  automobiles and there's a lot of  automobiles spread throughout the world  of course well not only is sulfur  dioxides  and nitrogen oxides released from  automobiles but also in  the reason industries around the world  when fossil fuels are burned usually in  the production of electricity and in  power to keep industry and factories  running but the the exhaust as you see  in this animation here tends to release  a lot of sulfur dioxides and nitrogen  oxides into the atmosphere and so what  are some effects of acid rain in nature  well number one it makes ecosystems more  acidic so as it rains you know the acids  you know wash into the rivers and in the  lakes and the ponds and are absorbed  into the soil of ecosystems around the  world  so as the pH is lowered into the harmful  acidic range this tends to hurt and harm  aquatic organisms such as fish  crustaceans and plankton that might  survive in these waterways and you know  here's some images of some you know dead  fish washed up because they were unable  to survive in the areas that were  affected most their habitat let's not  forget about the effects that this might  have on terrestrial life life that lives  on land as the pH of the soil is lowered  you know trees absorb these acids and  effects and phibian in the crop the  health of crops that are living within  the trying to be grown within an area  you know here we see some trees that  were harmed and damaged you can see the  trees are basically dead as they  absorbed the acids from the acid rain  you know there have been all kinds of  studies that have been done where crops  have been grown in areas with a lower  soil PH and the crops just generally  don't grow as well and therefore the  crop yield is much less and this could  harm of course you know the economic  benefits of that farmers enjoy when when  they grow their crops  and so how can acid rain be reduced well  well one of the things that we're seeing  is finding your figured out ways is to  neutralize the acidic soil and the  acidic waters of these ecosystems that  are affected the most and this picture  shows an act called Lyman where crushed  limestone is added to acidic soil in  this picture acidic soil and also in  acidic water ways to help help raise the  pH back to its normal level now this is  obviously only a temporary solution  because if acid rain continues in these  areas then liming will need to be  continued as well but limestone is helps  to counteract and bring up the pH to a  more healthy healthy range technology  has been used to help remove pollutants  from the air here we're looking at the  underside of an automobile at the  catalytic converter catalytic converters  will chemically change the exhaust of  the pollutants found in the exhaust of  automobiles at how it chemically changes  them into less harmful molecules also  industries in many cases have what are  called scrubbers on them and the  scrubber will remove pollutants from  industrial exhaust so as the exhaust  enters the scrubber the black dots are  representing of the pollutants the  pollutants are being basically filtered  out and when the exhaust comes out the  top end the pollutants have been removed  and so therefore the exhaust is a little  cleaner as it is released into the air  and into the ecosystem and let's not  forget well if burning fossil fuels is  one of the you know man-made causes of  acid rain then figuring out ways to  reduce our fossil fuel usage needs to be  explored coal oil natural gas for  they're not ways to become less  dependent upon these and so as we  explore alternative energy such as wind  energy and such as solar energy these  are ways that can hopefully limit the  use of fossil fuels as we try to produce  energy for our you know modern way of  life you know automobiles today are  becoming more fuel efficient not only  that but trying to refigure out ways to  you know become less dependent on them  such as carpooling and biking and more  fuel-efficient automobiles and public  transportation anything that we can do  to take some automobiles off of the road  should be viewed as a positive step  so for serious about reducing acid rain  then we really need to examine our  ability to reduce energy consumption  while at home and that would you know  require using more products that are  Energy Star labeled as they require less  power to be operated you know compact  fluorescent light bulbs use less energy  and therefore again reduce our use of  fossil fuels you know we're all guilty  from time to time of opening the  refrigerator door and staring into the  refrigerator and letting out the cool  energy but at the cool temperature but  when we do that it's a really poor use  of electricity and trying to avoid  situations like this you know also  trying to avoid those long 15 20 minu